<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  The resurrection core's automatic reload under Combat Extended: on, where the main tree
  leaves it off (the armor def's header has that default's reason). CE's players keep reload
  ammo in the loadout, and CE itself feeds every worn reloadable from the inventory before the
  map (CE 16.7.4, Harmony_JobGiver_Reload_TryGiveJob), so a pilot who walked past the components
  they carry to fetch others would read as broken there. A mod setting defaulting to this
  value, as in the main tree.

  The switch is all CE's reload needs in XML. Its prefix and its "Reload worn armor" button are
  met in C# (Source/1.6/Patches/JobGiver_Reload_TryGiveJob.cs, CompResurrectionCore's
  ForeignReloadCommand), and CE leaves ComponentSpacer, the reload's ammo, as vanilla has it.
-->
<Patch>
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName="OLWC_Warcasket_Overlord"]/comps/li[@Class="OverlordWarcasket.CompProperties_ResurrectionCore"]/autoReloadFromInventory</xpath>
    <value>
      <autoReloadFromInventory>true</autoReloadFromInventory>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
